-- title:
--   Freeness and rank m of Γ(V)/(g) for an m-th order neighbourhood
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local Noetherian ring, let $C$ be a scheme and let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, formalised as a pair consisting of a morphism $\varepsilon_1 : \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with a proof that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $c$ equals the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $m$ be a natural number with $m \ge 1$, let $V$ be an open subscheme of $C$ which is affine, assume that every point in the set-theoretic image of $\varepsilon_1$ lies in $V$, and let $g \in \Gamma(C, V)$. Assume that for every affine open $W$ of $C$ with $W \le V$, the ideal cut out at $W$ by the ideal sheaf datum $(\ker \varepsilon_1)^m$ is the principal ideal of $\Gamma(C, W)$ generated by the restriction of $g$ along $W \le V$. Then, for the $R$-algebra structure on $\Gamma(C, V)$ induced by $c$ (the composite of the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism with $c$'s map on sections from $\top$ to $V$), the quotient $\Gamma(C, V) / (g)$ is a free $R$-module and its rank over $R$ equals $m$.
--
--   This is the order-rank statement for the $m$-th infinitesimal neighbourhood $m\varepsilon$ of a section of a smooth proper relative curve: when the neighbourhood is contained in an affine open $V$ and its ideal is generated on $V$ by a single function $g$, the ring of the neighbourhood is $\Gamma(C,V)/(g)$, free of rank $m$ over the base. It is used in the construction of two-chart pole data from a section, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_of_section_invModule`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_of_section_invModule).
